{"hash":"ba763acfb556e801","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":89.238,"said":"You are inside the walls now, and before you rises Baba’s white tower. But how did he come to be here? The Shiva Purana tells of Ravana, the ten-headed king of Lanka, a great devotee of Shiva, and a proud one. In the forests below the Himalaya he dug a pit, lit the sacred fire, and worshipped Shiva through heat, rain and cold. Still Shiva did not come. So Ravana began to cut off his own heads, one by one, and offer them to the Lord. Nine heads fell. As he raised the sword to the tenth, Shiva appeared and set every head back in its place, without pain. Tradition says Shiva healed him as a physician heals, and so here he is Vaidyanath, Lord of Physicians. Ravana asked to carry Shiva’s linga home to Lanka. Shiva agreed, with one warning: wherever it is set on the ground, there it will stay. On the way Ravana had to stop, and gave the linga to a cowherd to hold. The cowherd waited, grew tired, and set it down. It never moved again. Many here say that cowherd was Vishnu himself, and call him Baiju. Now look up, at the red threads crossing the sky.\n\nDid you know? The Shiva Purana says that once the linga was fixed, Brahma, Vishnu and the other gods came to worship it, and named it Vaidyanatha.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1058},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1074,"end":1206}],"words":[[0.098,0.192,0,3],[0.302,0.132,4,7],[0.447,0.481,8,14],[0.939,0.12,15,18],[1.072,0.349,19,24],[1.432,0.349,25,28],[2.021,0.192,30,33],[2.225,0.361,34,40],[2.598,0.12,41,44],[2.73,0.481,45,50],[3.223,0.445,51,57],[3.68,0.288,58,63],[3.98,0.481,64,69],[5.324,0.156,71,74],[5.493,0.204,75,78],[5.709,0.168,79,82],[5.889,0.108,83,85],[6.01,0.252,86,90],[6.274,0.108,91,93],[6.394,0.144,94,96],[6.551,0.325,97,101],[7.728,0.108,103,106],[7.849,0.349,107,112],[8.209,0.493,113,119],[8.714,0.288,120,125],[9.014,0.144,126,128],[9.171,0.517,129,135],[9.928,0.12,137,140],[10.06,0.529,141,151],[1